"337\" y1=\"155.5\" x2=\"470\" y2=\"155.5\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><text x=\"475\" y=\"159.5\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\">Entry ~29.75</text><line x1=\"337\" y1=\"243.7\" x2=\"470\" y2=\"243.7\" stroke=\"#22c55e\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><text x=\"475\" y=\"247.7\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#22c55e\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\">T1: prior low 27.95</text><path d=\"M466,126 L460,126 L460,155.5 L466,155.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"454\" y=\"144.8\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#ef4444\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"600\">risk 0.60</text><path d=\"M466,155.5 L460,155.5 L460,243.7 L466,243.7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#22c55e\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"454\" y=\"203.6\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#22c55e\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"600\">reward 1.80 = 3:1</text><circle cx=\"329\" cy=\"135.9\" r=\"11\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><text x=\"313\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"600\">bearish candle, top</text><text x=\"313\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"600\">wick in the zone</text><text x=\"259\" y=\"194.7\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" text-anchor=\"end\">rapid rally</text><text x=\"259\" y=\"206.7\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" text-anchor=\"end\">into supply</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"350\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-style=\"italic\">Prices illustrative (zone 30.00-30.30 as in the MSFT example). For longs: bullish candle, lower wick in demand.</text></svg>",
    "caption": "With-trend swing short, modelled on Baker's MSFT chart. In a downtrend, price rallies quickly back into a supply zone and prints a bearish candle whose upper wick sits in the zone. Enter after that candle closes, stop a few cents above the top of the zone. Zone strength matters less here - the trend is the edge; the zone just has to exist."
